tioned verdict; T13-R2 additionally reads `subpartition_name` per row — any non-null leaf name marks the top-level directory incomplete (`PartitionNames=nil`), so leaf members are never claimed proven-absent (MySQL catalogs leaf names and exchanges them; TiDB normalizes the clause away and keeps NULL — issue #92 T13-R1/R2). T14 additionally reads `partition_description` per member (aligned `PartitionDescriptions` → `spec.CatalogPartitionDefs` bound projection, NULL/empty on HASH|KEY members kept as empty text rather than unobserved) and exposes the leaf-row marker on `snapshot.Subpartitioned` so consumers distinguish an incomplete projection from an unanswered probe (issue #93 T14) `Provider.ResolveObject` resolves schema identities through `information_schema.SCHEMATA` (existence, default charset/collation, capability-probed `DEFAULT_ENCRYPTION` on MySQL 8.0.16+, TiDB `TIDB_PLACEMENT_POLICY_NAME`); other object types report unavailable rather than fabricating coverage (issue #96 T17) |
